# nr-office-comrs-ppt-edit: the PowerPoint editor of mixdog-office-com (src/ppt/edit/{mod,layout,text,shapes,tables,images,slides,footer,
# template,chart_data,chart_window,charts}.rs: Apply-PowerPointOperation, its 46 operations, the chart data sheet with its Excel process
# tracking and the hidden chart window), tests/ppt_edit.rs, tests/ppt_edit_live.rs, recorder/scenarios/ppt-edit.json and
# tests/fixtures/ppt-edit/inputs/{pixel.png,tone.wav}.
# Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave); the sources were checked to parse with rustfmt only.
# No protocol row, no service, no SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to this task. No new dependency edge and no new crate: the code uses
# only what the crate has (regex, zip for the live test, the crate's own com, ps, platform, state and template modules).
# This task builds on the PowerPoint reader (nr-office-comrs-ppt-read: src/ppt/{mod,ink,...}.rs), whose own fragment adds `pub mod ppt;`
# to lib.rs; apply that one first.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/ppt/mod.rs (not owned by this task)
The editor is used by the integration tests and by the driver table, so the module is public: replace

    pub(crate) mod edit;

by

    pub mod edit;

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/drivers.rs (not owned by this task)
Register the editor: replace the empty `EDITORS` table by (keep the doc comment above it, and the lines the Word and Excel editors add)

    static EDITORS: &[(&str, &dyn FormatEditor)] = &[("pptx", &crate::ppt::edit::Editor)];

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (not owned by this task)
Test targets, after `[[test]] name = "actions_live"` (and the ppt_read ones):

    [[test]]
    name = "ppt_edit"
    path = "tests/ppt_edit.rs"

    [[test]]
    name = "ppt_edit_live"
    path = "tests/ppt_edit_live.rs"

## 4. Two helpers the script shares with the other editors
`Office-ChartTypeCode` (the chart type by name or code) and `Provenance-Text` are shared by the three editors in office-com-host.ps1.
This task needed them and the Word and Excel editors are written in parallel, so each is written once here, as `pub(crate)`:
`crate::ppt::edit::charts::chart_type_code(&crate::ps::Value) -> crate::com::Result<i32>` and
`crate::ppt::edit::slides::provenance_text(&crate::ps::Value) -> crate::com::Result<String>`.
nr-office-comrs-excel-edit (add_chart, set_chart_series, ...) and nr-office-comrs-word-edit (add_provenance) must call these and not
carry a second copy; if either already wrote its own, delete that copy and point it here (or move both to a shared module, which is the
lead's call: no other file of this task changes).

## 5. After the recording
`node recorder/record-office-com.mjs --area ppt-edit` (on the migration PC with Microsoft PowerPoint and Excel) writes
tests/fixtures/ppt-edit/<scenario>.json and updates tests/fixtures/MANIFEST.json; `recorded_scenarios_are_replayed` of tests/ppt_edit.rs
replays every operation of every recorded batch (it passes without a fixture and says so). The first replay may need the platform script
adjusted: the test puts one fake window on the fake platform per window handle the recorded log read (a process of its own each) and
no Excel process before the operation, which is what the registry of the chart Excel is exercised with.
